			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tuzEtMfPy1CevZpYw",
			"name": "Grey Knight Lens: Interceptor",
			"local_notes": "Disabled by default; enable only for a Grey Knight posted to an Interceptor squad (teleport-strike deep insertion).\n\nLore: Interceptor squads are the Grey Knights' rapid-response arm, teleporting directly into a daemonic incursion's midst rather than advancing on foot, per Codex: Grey Knights background and Ben Counter's novels' recurring \"Grey Knights translate directly into the heart of the fighting\" beat.\n\nDesign: Rather than invent a new short-range teleport mechanic, this lens is built identically to Telekinesis's own Gate of Infinity (Imperium/Traits/Psykers and the Warp.adq: Basic's Warp advantage, B99, flat 100, with Preparation Required -20%, Warp Sorcery -20%, and Severe Perils -20%, net -60%) -- an Interceptor's teleport strike is mechanically the same instant-translocation power a Librarian's Gate of Infinity is, just trained into every Brother of this squad role rather than one specialist. Full modified cost: 100 x 0.4 = 40 points; it needs Warp Empowerment level 3 (cap 40) -- exactly this add-on's baseline level, so enabling this lens uses the full width of the psychic gift's cap with no headroom to spare, appropriate for a squad role built entirely around one demanding, high-risk power.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Psyker",
				"Imperium",
				"Grey Knights",
				"Chapter Variant"
			],
			"modifiers": [
				{
					"id": "mIEA5GDmWKCNcyFPu",
					"name": "Preparation Required",
					"cost_adj": "-20%"
				},
				{
					"id": "mCuJ7fiCaRoxgaT9N",
					"name": "Warp Sorcery",
					"cost_adj": "-20%"
				},
				{
					"id": "mFB-uwEi7i1k3sfcP",
					"name": "Perils of the Warp (Severe)",
					"cost_adj": "-20%"
				}
			],
			"base_points": 100,
			"disabled": true
		},
		{
			"id": "TUVeIAerOmrTOkDb0",
			"name": "Grey Knight Lens: Paladin",
			"local_notes": "Disabled by default; enable only for a veteran Grey Knight elevated to the Paladin cadre (Terminator-armoured elite, see Aegis Terminator Armour, Imperium/Grey Knights/Grey Knights Wargear.eqp).\n\nLore: Paladins are the Grey Knights' most veteran Brothers, fighting permanently in Terminator plate against the worst things the Chapter faces; Codex: Grey Knights background treats elevation to the Paladin cadre as a mark of survival and trust on top of the standard Battle-Brother training every Grey Knight already has.\n\nDesign: One further level of Rank (B29, 5 points/level, matching the Battle-Brother template's own Rank 3 entry in Astartes Gene-Seed.adq's parent template) plus Extra Hit Points +1 (B16, 2/level) for the additional hardening veteran survival buys, 5 + 2 = 7 points -- a modest bump reflecting individual seniority on top of the shared Grey Knight package, not a second racial template.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium",
				"Grey Knights",
				"Chapter Variant"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tJSqQoNEHZO4p3pFD",
					"name": "Rank 1 (Grey Knight Paladin)",
					"reference": "B29",
					"base_points": 5
				},
				{
					"id": "tSiERwGuxkahIOkF_",
					"name": "Extra Hit Points",
					"reference": "B16",
					"points_per_level": 2,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 1
				}
			],
			"disabled": true
		}
	],
	"skills": [
		{
			"id": "sbSP0mrq4g_dUN_TA",
			"name": "Meditation",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Every Grey Knight drills the same discipline the Astartes Librarian Add-On's own Meditation entry (Imperium/Templates/Astartes Librarian Add-On.gct) describes, to hold his gift steady in the presence of the warp's worst.\n\nDesign: Meditation is Will/Hard (B207); points as the Librarian Add-On's own identical entry.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Psyker",
				"Grey Knights"
			],
			"difficulty": "will/h",
			"points": 4
		},
		{
			"id": "sS9HqxB4d7R7XRQsy",
			"name": "Hidden Lore",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Grey Knight's formal Sanctic training in the immaterium's nature, matching the Librarian Add-On's identical entry.\n\nDesign: Easy skill (B198); points as the Librarian Add-On's own identical entry.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Psyker",
				"Grey Knights"
			],
			"specialization": "the Warp",
			"difficulty": "iq/a",
			"points": 4
		},
		{
			"id": "sbmIoW1sb9Iz6m4Wb",
			"name": "Hidden Lore",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Grey Knights exist to hunt daemons, and Codex: Grey Knights background is explicit that the Chapter's knowledge of daemonic nature, names and weaknesses outstrips even the Inquisition's Ordo Malleus in places -- a Grey Knight's Hidden Lore (Daemons) is expected to be exceptional, not merely competent the way a line Battle-Brother's (Astartes Gene-Seed.adq's Battle-Brother template already has a lesser Hidden Lore, Xenos and Heresy, at 8 and 2 points respectively).\n\nDesign: 16 points on an IQ/Average skill is enough for roughly IQ+3 or better at a Grey Knight's typical IQ, a specialist's mastery rather than the field-competence level (8 points, roughly IQ+1) this project gives a line Battle-Brother's Hidden Lore specialisations.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Psyker",
				"Grey Knights"
			],
			"specialization": "Daemons",
			"difficulty": "iq/a",
			"points": 16
		},
		{
			"id": "skc_gkE_0HFFLaD0D",
			"name": "Polearm",
			"local_notes": "Nemesis Force Halberd (Imperium/Gear/Psychic Gear.eqp).\n\nLore: The Nemesis Force Halberd is the Chapter's signature weapon, and most Grey Knights are trained to use one from their earliest live drills.\n\nDesign: Average skill, a trained specialist's level; the Battle-Brother base template has no Polearm skill of its own.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Psyker",
				"Grey Knights"
			],
			"difficulty": "dx/a",
			"points": 8
		},
		{
			"id": "sSrQQDUS7bc9g_Js8",
			"name": "Two-Handed Axe/Mace",
			"local_notes": "Nemesis Daemon Hammer (Imperium/Grey Knights/Grey Knights Wargear.eqp).\n\nLore: Carried by Grey Knights who favour crushing force over the halberd's reach, especially among Terminator-armoured Paladins.\n\nDesign: Average skill; the Battle-Brother base template's Axe/Mace entry (2 points, chainaxe familiarity) is a different, lighter weapon class.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Psyker",
				"Grey Knights"
			],
			"difficulty": "dx/a",
			"points": 8
		},
		{
			"id": "s58IdoXmx0_ZIJ-tU",
			"name": "Staff",
			"local_notes": "Warding Stave (Imperium/Grey Knights/Grey Knights Wargear.eqp).\n\nLore: Carried by Grey Knights who lead a kill-team's wardings, per Imperium/Grey Knights/Grey Knights Wargear.eqp's own entry.\n\nDesign: Average skill at familiarity level; not every Grey Knight carries a stave, so this is priced lightly compared with Polearm above.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Psyker",
				"Grey Knights"
			],
			"difficulty": "dx/a",
			"points": 4
		},
		{
			"id": "sQlSaArAnR4tYl6ss",
			"name": "Gunner",
			"local_notes": "Psycannon and Psilencer (Imperium/Grey Knights/Grey Knights Wargear.eqp), per the framework's \"braced/mounted heavies -> Gunner\" skill rule.\n\nDesign: Average skill; the Battle-Brother base template has Guns (Rifle/Pistol) but no Gunner skill, which the Chapter's own heavy weapons need.",
