	"equipment": [
		{
			"id": "EiqI9_XlDtRgsv3mI",
			"description": "Aegis Power Armour",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 4: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 4 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it. Gap DR: arm 35, leg 35.\n\nRequires the black carapace interface, as Mark VII. The Aegis conditional bonus stacks with the wearer's own Rites of Sanctity (Imperium/Traits/Grey Knights.adq) and with a carried Psychic Hood or Hexagrammic Ward Charm (Imperium/Gear/Psychic Gear.eqp).\n\nLore: Codex: Grey Knights and Ben Counter's novels describe Grey Knight power armour as Mark VII-class plate every plate and seal of which is inlaid with silver hexagrammic wards, anointed and re-sanctified by the Chapter's own Interrogator-Chaplains, so that the armour itself resists possession and daemonic influence rather than relying on the wearer's own soul alone — a second line of defence on top of what a Grey Knight's body already is (see Grey Knight Soul, Imperium/Traits/ Grey Knights.adq).\n\nDesign: Torso DR, weak_points, eye-lens DR, and servo-motor ST bonus are taken unchanged from the Mark VII (Aquila Pattern) baseline (Imperium/ Armour/Imperial Armour.eqp): the anchor table lore is explicit that Grey Knight plate is a warded Mark VII derivative, not a physically thicker suit — the Chapter's edge against daemons is spiritual, not a bigger DR number, so this entry deliberately does not invent a new physical-DR anchor. What's added is the conditional_modifier feature (same mechanic as the Psychic Hood item, Imperium/Gear/Psychic Gear.eqp): a flat +3 to resist Warp Sorcery-tagged mental attacks and possession directed at the wearer, one point higher than the Psychic Hood's +2 since this is inscribed across an entire suit of plate rather than a single circlet. Cost is more than doubled over the Mark VII baseline (40000) to reflect the labour of a full-suit sanctification rite (Ordo Malleus- and Chapter-restricted, hence the LC0 and the superscience ^ TL tag alongside the standard TL11 power-armour bracket) rather than a material or servo upgrade; weight, attribute bonuses and every other figure are otherwise identical to Mark VII.",
			"tags": [
				"Body Armor",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes",
				"Grey Knights"
			],
