			"quantity": 1,
			"equipped": true,
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "eM__fo9bcZZLQct0k",
					"description": "Auto-senses Suite",
					"local_notes": "As the Mark VII Auto-senses Suite (threat auto-cueing, low-light and audio filtering); requires the black carapace interface for full effect.\n\nLore: The Aegis plate is a warded Mark VII derivative and keeps the standard Astartes sensor package.\n\nDesign: Same figures as the Mark VII child (Imperium/Armour/Imperial Armour.eqp); GCS adds a container's children to its own weight and cost, so the shell carries 146 lb and $84,000 and the assembled suit still totals 150 lb and $90,000.",
					"base_value": "6000",
					"base_weight": "4 lb",
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "skill_bonus",
