		{
			"id": "eTXtimppixxkB7IKu",
			"description": "Nemesis Force Sword",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The standard one-handed Nemesis weapon pattern, carried where a Grey Knight favours reach and a guard over the Nemesis Force Halberd's two-handed heft; Ben Counter's Grey Knights novels show it as the Chapter's most common sidearm-grade Nemesis weapon after the halberd itself.\n\nDesign: Astartes Power Sword pattern (Imperium/Weapons/Melee Weapons.eqp): field-off is the plain Astartes-scale broadsword baseline (sw+1 cut), field-on adds the shared power-field rule's +3d and Armor Divisor (10) (framework.md), at the same weight (9 lb) and min ST (16) as that entry, since a Nemesis blade's extra sanctification and psychic attunement change what it can do to a daemon, not its physical mass or handling. Exact dice distribution at full Astartes ST 30 (sw 5d+2 per B16, so field-on totals 8d+3(10) cut, average 31): penetrates carapace (DR 70), Sororitas power armour (DR 85), and Astartes power armour (DR 100) essentially always (100% by exact distribution) and Terminator plate (DR 200, eff. DR 20) 98.6% of the time — matching \"the disruption field shears power armour whoever holds it\" at the high end of this project's power-weapon family. The Force Strike line reuses the Nemesis Force Halberd's waived-Perils convention (Imperium/Gear/Psychic Gear.eqp): every Nemesis weapon is permanently attuned for anti-daemon work, so a Grey Knight needs no check to use it against the enemy this weapon exists for. LC0 (Grey Knights- and Ordo Malleus-restricted, per the framework's legality table) and superscience TL10^ (warp-attuned, like every other force weapon in Imperium/Gear/Psychic Gear.eqp), priced above the generic Force Sword (8000, Imperium/Gear/Psychic Gear.eqp) for the Chapter's own sanctification rites on top of the Astartes-scale housing.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Psyker",
				"Grey Knights"
			],
