		{
			"id": "e4V9y8TxBK3hTCAgl",
			"description": "Psybolt Ammunition",
			"local_notes": "A full magazine load, statted as loaded into a Boltgun, Godwyn Pattern or Storm Bolter (matching that weapon's own handling figures above, RoF 3x2 and ST 20 for the twin-linked storm bolter); use this weapon block in place of the host weapon's Standard bolt line while loaded.\n\nLore: Grey Knights load their boltguns and storm bolters with rounds cast from psychically-reactive, sanctified alloys and blessed over weeks of ritual before a campaign, described in Codex: Grey Knights background as hitting noticeably harder than a standard bolt round against armoured foes and daemonic constructs alike, without changing the weapon that fires them.\n\nDesign: Same dice and wounding modifier as the standard Godwyn-anchor bolt (6dx2(2) pi++, Imperium/Weapons/Bolt Weapons.eqp) with the armour divisor raised one step to (3), the same divisor-only change the Kraken penetrator round already uses on the same page, representing a denser sanctified penetrator core rather than a new cartridge. Exact dice distribution against Astartes power armour (DR 100, eff. DR 33.3): penetrates 85.5% of hits, up from the standard round's 14.5% — the \"hits noticeably harder against armoured foes\" the lore describes — while carapace (DR 70, eff. 23.3) and Sororitas armour (DR 85, eff. 28.3) both round to essentially 100%. Handling figures are not restated as their own weapon: this is ammunition for an existing gun, so weight and cost are for one spare magazine's worth, priced above plain bolt rounds for the sanctification labour, and TL is marked superscience (10^) like this project's other warp-touched consumables despite riding in an ordinary TL10 weapon.",
